# Blueprint Agent Architecture

## Overview

The Smart Claim Blueprint Generator will operate as a pre-submission intelligence layer that evaluates claim quality and provides recommendations before the user finalizes a claim. This proactive approach will significantly improve claim quality and streamline the RMA process.

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[User Initiates Claim] --> B[Data Collection]
    B --> C[Pre-Submission Trigger]
    C --> D[Blueprint Agent]
    D --> E1[memoryTracker]
    D --> E2[anomalyDetector]
    D --> E3[contextBuilder]
    D --> E4[orgLearningVault]
    D --> E5[recommendationEngine]
    E1 --> F[Blueprint Generation]
    E2 --> F
    E3 --> F
    E4 --> F
    E5 --> F
    F --> G[Blueprint Storage]
    F --> H[UI Feedback]
    H --> I[User Completes/Enhances Claim]
    I --> J[Final Submission]
    J --> K[Vendor Form Auto-fill]
```

## Core Components

1. **Pre-Submission Trigger**
   - Activates when user has entered initial claim details but before finalization
   - Threshold: At least one photo + basic issue description entered

2. **MCP7 Integration Points**
   - Connects to existing intelligence layers
   - Uses contextBuilder to analyze equipment-specific requirements
   - Leverages orgLearningVault for historical claim patterns
   - Utilizes anomalyDetector to identify missing critical information
   - Integrates with recommendationEngine for suggesting improvements

3. **Blueprint Generator Core**
   - Evaluates completeness, accuracy, and quality
   - Generates structured recommendation object
   - Calculates confidence score (0-100%)
   - Identifies claim enhancement opportunities

4. **Real-time UI Integration**
   - Returns blueprint via API to mobile frontend
   - Displays visual checklist and improvement suggestions
   - Updates dynamically as user enhances claim

